00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:29.240
A, a cozy, is it a cozy game?

00:20:29.400 --> 00:20:34.280
Is it a, uh, like a vibe game where it's like, yeah, I just want to chill out and do some supercars.

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:40.060
Like what is, cause these racing games all have to kind of like sell a mood more than anything.

00:20:40.220 --> 00:20:44.400
Right. Like stylistically, that's where all these racing games set each other apart.

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:55.140
What's more aesthetic and mood than going into a sales office where you talk to a guy, uh, in a gray suit while his secretary works in the background.

00:20:55.480 --> 00:21:02.280
Uh, but it, but that was immersion breaking for me, Sean, because the dealer wouldn't sell me a car worse than my own.

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:06.060
He was like, oh, you already have a better car than this.

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:08.940
Oh. And it's like, um, excuse me.

